@startuml example-train-eval
' The end-to-end train → fuse → evaluate → persist workflow walked by
' docs/examples/train-and-evaluate.md. Colour encodes the component that owns each
' stage (repo-wide legend in architecture.puml): corpora / external crates (grey),
' statistical LM core (blue), embeddings (green), hybrid fusion (steel blue),
' applications & evaluation (slate), storage / persistence (teal).
' Render: plantuml -tsvg docs/diagrams/example-train-eval.puml
' Source of truth for Figure 1 in docs/examples/train-and-evaluate.md §2
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam rectangle {
  FontColor white
  FontStyle bold
  BorderColor #263238
  roundCorner 12
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
title Train → fuse → evaluate → persist  (one reader per training pass)

rectangle "**corpus.txt**\nplain text on disk" as corpus #546E7A
rectangle "**PlaintextReader::from_file**\nNormalizer: NFC · control chars · whitespace\nTokenizer: lowercase · sentences on [.!?]+␣" as reader #546E7A

rectangle "**TrainerBuilder::new(dict).order(n)**\n① count n-grams (Rayon · atomic entries)\n② continuation counts N₁₊(•,w), N₁₊(h,•)\n③ discounts D₁ D₂ D₃₊ from n₁…n₄" as ngtrain #1565C0
rectangle "**NgramModel<D>**\nlog_prob(w, h) · sentence_log_prob(s)\nModified Kneser-Ney · O(n) look-ups" as ngram #1565C0

rectangle "**EmbeddingTrainerBuilder**\ndim · window_size · min_count · epochs\nskip-gram + negative sampling" as emtrain #2E7D32
rectangle "**SubwordEmbedding**\nword_vector · similarity · most_similar\nhashed character n-grams ⇒ OOV coverage" as embed #2E7D32

rectangle "**HybridLanguageModel::new(ngram, embedding, cfg)**\nscore(w, h) = α·ℙₙ ⊕ (1−α)·ℙₑ\nInterpolationStrategy · lock-free score cache" as hybrid #1B6CA8

rectangle "**Perplexity::new(&ngram)**\n.corpus_perplexity(&test_reader)\nPP · OOV rate · token & sentence counts" as eval #455A64
rectangle "**persist** (feature `serde-extras`)\nsave / load — needs D: Serialize\nsave_portable / load_portable — any backend" as persist #00838F

corpus --> reader
reader --> ngtrain : reader moved **by value**\n(pass 1)
reader --> emtrain : a **second** reader\n(pass 2)
ngtrain --> ngram
emtrain --> embed
ngram --> hybrid
embed --> hybrid
ngram --> eval : baseline PP
hybrid --> eval : fused PP
ngram --> persist
hybrid --> persist

note bottom of reader #ECEFF1
  CorpusReader::sentences() **streams**;
  train() **consumes** its reader, so
  build a fresh one for every pass.
end note

note right of eval #E3F2FD
  Perplexity wraps an **NgramModel**.
  Score a hybrid with
  HybridLanguageModel::perplexity
  (per sentence) — see §8.
end note

@enduml
